§§ `Annex I, section A — the class of a vehicle, and its premium`

-- IV, by seats: under 6; 6 to 11; 12 to 24; over 24. The four bands meet with no gap and no
-- overlap for a whole number of seats.
GIVEN seats IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Annex I A.IV — a car not used for transport business, of` seats MEANS
    BRANCH IF seats LESS THAN 6  THEN `Annex I A.IV.1 — a car under 6 seats`
           IF seats AT MOST   11 THEN `Annex I A.IV.2 — a car of 6 to 11 seats`
           IF seats AT MOST   24 THEN `Annex I A.IV.3 — a car of 12 to 24 seats`
           OTHERWISE               `Annex I A.IV.4 — a car over 24 seats`

-- V, by registered seats: one row per number of seats from 6 to 25, a row for fewer than 6 and
-- a formula for more than 25.
GIVEN seats IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Annex I A.V — a car used for transport business, of` seats MEANS
    BRANCH IF seats LESS THAN 6  THEN `Annex I A.V.1 — under 6 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    6  THEN `Annex I A.V.2 — 6 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    7  THEN `Annex I A.V.3 — 7 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    8  THEN `Annex I A.V.4 — 8 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    9  THEN `Annex I A.V.5 — 9 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    10 THEN `Annex I A.V.6 — 10 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    11 THEN `Annex I A.V.7 — 11 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    12 THEN `Annex I A.V.8 — 12 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    13 THEN `Annex I A.V.9 — 13 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    14 THEN `Annex I A.V.10 — 14 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    15 THEN `Annex I A.V.11 — 15 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    16 THEN `Annex I A.V.12 — 16 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    17 THEN `Annex I A.V.13 — 17 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    18 THEN `Annex I A.V.14 — 18 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    19 THEN `Annex I A.V.15 — 19 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    20 THEN `Annex I A.V.16 — 20 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    21 THEN `Annex I A.V.17 — 21 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    22 THEN `Annex I A.V.18 — 22 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    23 THEN `Annex I A.V.19 — 23 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    24 THEN `Annex I A.V.20 — 24 registered seats`
           IF seats EQUALS    25 THEN `Annex I A.V.21 — 25 registered seats`
           IF seats GREATER THAN 25 THEN `Annex I A.V.22 — over 25 seats, for` seats
           OTHERWISE `a number of seats Annex I section V does not list is not encoded in this model`

-- A number of seats that is not a whole number falls between the rows of section V. Seats
-- are counted in whole numbers on a registration; this is a guard, not a reading.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a number of seats Annex I section V does not list is not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "a number of seats Annex I section V does not list is not encoded in this model"

-- VI, by payload: under 3 tonnes; 3 to 8; over 8 to 15; over 15. The bands meet with no gap.
GIVEN tonnes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Annex I A.VI — a goods vehicle of payload` tonnes MEANS
    BRANCH IF tonnes LESS THAN 3  THEN `Annex I A.VI.1 — under 3 tonnes`
           IF tonnes AT MOST   8  THEN `Annex I A.VI.2 — from 3 to 8 tonnes`
           IF tonnes AT MOST   15 THEN `Annex I A.VI.3 — over 8 to 15 tonnes`
           OTHERWISE                `Annex I A.VI.4 — over 15 tonnes`

-- VII. Other cases. Each is a percentage of a row of IV, V or VI.
